      "text": "Function-by-Function Flow\n\nhandleOtpSuccess(otp) (App.jsx): Triggered when the user submits the code. Sets isLoading = true and calls authService.verifyOtp({ email: pendingEmail, otp }).\nauthService.verifyOtp() (api.js): Passes the payload to your core request() helper.\nrequest() (api.js): Sends an HTTP POST request to /api/auth/verify-otp with { email, otp } in the body.\nrouter.post('/verify-otp') (authRoutes.js): Catches the route and calls the verifyOtp controller function.\nverifyOtp() (authController.js):\nCalls User.findOne({ email }) in MongoDB.\nCompares user.verifyOtp !== String(otp) and checks Date.now() > user.verifyOtpExpireAt.\nSets user.isAccountVerified = true, clears user.verifyOtp = null, and runs await user.save().\nbuildUserPayload(user) (authController.js): Converts the MongoDB user document into a safe JSON object and calls generateToken().\ngenerateToken(payload) (authController.js): Calls jwt.sign(tokenPayload, secret, { expiresIn: '30d' }). This cryptographically seals the user's id, name, email, and role into a single JWT string.\nres.json() (authController.js): Returns the user object along with the new token string back to the frontend.\npersistToken(result) (api.js): Runs window.localStorage.setItem('paper_path_token', token).\nhandleOtpSuccess() (App.jsx): Runs setUser(verifiedUser) and setView('dashboard'). The user is now fully authenticated.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Function-by-Function Flow\n\nhandleOtpSuccess(otp) (App.jsx): Triggered when the user submits the code. Sets isLoading = true and calls authService.verifyOtp({ email: pendingEmail, otp }).\nauthService.verifyOtp() (api.js): Passes the payload to your core request() helper.\nrequest() (api.js): Sends an HTTP POST request to /api/auth/verify-otp with { email, otp } in the body.\nrouter.post('/verify-otp') (authRoutes.js): Catches the route and calls the verifyOtp controller function.\nverifyOtp() (authController.js):\nCalls User.findOne({ email }) in MongoDB.\nCompares user.verifyOtp !== String(otp) and checks Date.now() > user.verifyOtpExpireAt.\nSets user.isAccountVerified = true, clears user.verifyOtp = null, and runs await user.save().\nbuildUserPayload(user) (authController.js): Converts the MongoDB user document into a safe JSON object and calls generateToken().\ngenerateToken(payload) (authController.js): Calls jwt.sign(tokenPayload, secret, { expiresIn: '30d' }). This cryptographically seals the user's id, name, email, and role into a single JWT string.\nres.json() (authController.js): Returns the user object along with the new token string back to the frontend.\npersistToken(result) (api.js): Runs window.localStorage.setItem('paper_path_token', token).\nhandleOtpSuccess() (App.jsx): Runs setUser(verifiedUser) and setView('dashboard'). The user is now fully authenticated.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
